  "question": {
    "text": "Conductor wire ABCDE with each $\\operatorname{arm} 10 \\mathrm{~cm}$ in length is placed in magnetic field of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$ Tesla, perpendicular to its plane. When conductor is pulled towards right with constant velocity of $10 \\mathrm{~cm} / \\mathrm{s}$, induced emf between points A and E is _____ mV.<br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/FPVR5p89HZQbfccK6XuxSUaSRb1KGiFdcHIWE757RQo.original.fullsize.png\"/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8biWp_JVSPTg-g3lgRlZJFlQSFjByYvEK4fFQOe4J5g.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>As field is uniform we can replace the bent wire with straight wire from $A$ to $B$.<br/>So EMF :<br/>$\\varepsilon=\\mathrm{Bv} \\ell_{\\mathrm{AB}}$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\times \\frac{10 \\mathrm{~cm}}{5} \\times 2\\left(10 \\sin 45^{\\circ}\\right) \\mathrm{cm} \\\\ & \\varepsilon=10 \\mathrm{mV}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
